  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia-Malaysia Reform Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia-Malaysia Reform Partnership (AMRP) between DFAT and The Asia Foundation (TAF) is the successor program to the Malaysia and Thailand Reform Partnerships. The AMRP is a small, flexible program aimed at supporting meaningful progress on policy reforms in Malaysia which will be critical for maintaining inclusive growth and stability. Acknowledging that reform in priority policy areas is complex and takes time, the AMRP will ensure that important reforms we commenced during the MTRP continue and can be deepened, as well as allowing for new areas of reform cooperation to be explored.  AMRP focus areas include supporting Care Economy reforms to boost women&apos;s workforce participation, and Blue Economy initiatives in Sabah.</narrative>
  </description>
